  "description": "Proposed erection of a two-storey side extension, part two-storey part single-storey rear extension, rear dormer roof extension with front extension and basement extension which accompany this application have been designed carefully around the outcomes and advice of previous associated applications, including appeal responses and pre-application advice. These appear in the Council’s records as follows:\n\nRefused appeal notice by the Secretary of State’s Patrick Whelan, with reference:\nAPP/L5810/D/20/3258950. This appeal refusal notice provided detailed notes for what I needed to revise in the latest plans. \n\nTo overcome any potential ambiguity and risk of another rejection, I applied for Pre-Application Advice (with reference: 24/P0150/PREAPP) using the revised plans dictated by the above. The council’s advice has been applied to my latest plans. \n\nFurther, I conducted a detailed study of local planning approvals, in and around the immediate area, to ensure this application meets the council’s expectations towards approval. \n\nI have dissected each point afforded by the above and addressed them individually on the proposed plans, with notes, to aid the assigned Planning Officer as best I can. \n\nI expect this application will now successfully meet the planning laws as they stand today, in addition to Richmond Council's latest Local Plan recommendations. \n",
